    "updated_at": "2026-11-17T14:51:23Z",
    "body": "Not fixed in PR #2353. The sources disagree, so G73 stays as on main. This issue is blocked until the maintainer decides.\n\n- The maintainer chose \"Post P as on G83\" for G73. His control check (840D, ISO dialect mode G291) was for G83 only.\n- Siemens' ISO dialects Function Manual (07/2021), section 6.3, table 6-2, lists no P on G73 (format X Y Z R F Q). G73 calls the shell cycle CYCLE383M. The manual lists the dwell at final depth only for G82, G89, G76 and G87.\n- Siemens document 109783242 was named by the maintainer, not read (the page needs JavaScript).\n\nOptions for the maintainer:\n1. Post P on G73 (his dialog choice). A control check of G73 with P would confirm it.\n2. Refuse a G73 dwell by name with `msg()`.\n\nMain still drops a G73 dwell without a diagnostic. The same pattern in four other posts is #2356.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
